$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"ZealOS Network Stack"$$FG$
$FG,2$$TX+CX,"TLS 1.3, HTTPS, WebSocket, and Discord API"$$FG$

$HD+CX,"Overview"$

This network stack provides TLS 1.3 encrypted communication for ZealOS,
enabling secure HTTPS requests, WebSocket connections, and Discord bot
functionality.

$HD+CX,"Architecture"$

$FG,3$Crypto/$FG$      - Cryptographic primitives
  SHA256.ZC     - SHA-256 hash function
  SHA512.ZC     - SHA-384/SHA-512 hash functions
  HMAC.ZC       - HMAC-SHA256/SHA384
  HKDF.ZC       - HKDF key derivation
  AES.ZC        - AES-128/256 block cipher
  GCM.ZC        - Galois/Counter Mode AEAD
  X25519.ZC     - Curve25519 ECDH
  Random.ZC     - CSPRNG

$FG,3$TLS/$FG$         - TLS 1.3 protocol
  TLSRecord.ZC    - Record layer
  TLSHandshake.ZC - Full handshake

$FG,3$HTTP/$FG$        - HTTP/HTTPS client
  HTTPClient.ZC   - HTTP/1.1 client

$FG,3$WebSocket/$FG$   - WebSocket client
  WebSocketClient.ZC - RFC 6455 WebSocket

$FG,3$Discord/$FG$     - Discord API
  DiscordJSON.ZC   - JSON builder/parser
  DiscordClient.ZC - Gateway + REST API
  ExampleBot.ZC    - Example bot

$HD+CX,"Quick Start"$

Load the network stack:
  #include "C:/Home/Net/MakeNet"

Run crypto tests:
  SHA256Test();
  AESTest();
  GCMTest();
  X25519Test();

Make an HTTPS request:
  CHTTPResponse *resp = HTTPGet("https://example.com");
  if (resp) {
    "%s\n", resp->body;
    HTTPResponseFree(resp);
  }

Run a Discord bot:
  ExampleBotRun("YOUR_BOT_TOKEN");

$HD+CX,"Discord Bot Example"$

  U0 MyOnReady(CDiscordClient *client, CDiscordUser *user)
  {
    "Connected as %s!\n", user->username;
  }

  U0 MyOnMessage(CDiscordClient *client, CDiscordMessage *msg)
  {
    if (msg->author.bot) return;

    if (StrNCmp(msg->content, "!hello", 6) == 0) {
      DiscordReplyMessage(client, msg, "Hello!");
    }
  }

  U0 MyBot(U8 *token)
  {
    CDiscordClient *client = DiscordInit(token);
    DiscordSetIntents(client, DISCORD_INTENTS_DEFAULT |
                              DISCORD_INTENT_MESSAGE_CONTENT);
    DiscordOnReady(client, &MyOnReady);
    DiscordOnMessage(client, &MyOnMessage);
    DiscordRun(client);
    DiscordCleanup(client);
  }

$HD+CX,"Supported Features"$

$FG,2$Crypto:$FG$
- SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512
- HMAC-SHA256, HMAC-SHA384
- HKDF (RFC 5869)
- AES-128-GCM, AES-256-GCM
- X25519 ECDH
- CSPRNG (SHA-256 based)

$FG,2$TLS 1.3:$FG$
- Full handshake
- X25519 key exchange
- AES-128-GCM cipher suite
- SNI extension
- Encrypted records

$FG,2$HTTP:$FG$
- HTTP/1.1 over TLS
- GET, POST, PUT, DELETE
- Chunked encoding
- Keep-alive connections

$FG,2$WebSocket:$FG$
- RFC 6455 compliant
- WSS (secure WebSocket)
- Text and binary frames
- Ping/pong handling
- Fragmentation support

$FG,2$Discord:$FG$
- Gateway WebSocket connection
- Heartbeat handling
- Event dispatch (READY, MESSAGE_CREATE)
- REST API for sending messages
- Auto-reconnect

$HD+CX,"Limitations"$

- No certificate validation (trusts all servers)
- Single cipher suite (AES-128-GCM-SHA256)
- No client certificates
- No session resumption (PSK)
- Minimal Discord API coverage
- Not thread-safe

